# monitor-core configuration — the COMPLETE set of variables this binary reads.
#
# Pinned by env/env_example_test.go: every name env.go/role.go reads must appear
# here, and every name here must be one they read. The file this replaced listed
# API_KEY, which nothing has ever read, and omitted all fourteen MON_* variables
# — i.e. every variable capable of failing the boot.
#
# Values below are the code's own defaults unless marked. A variable with no
# default is marked REQUIRED and its absence stops the process.

# ─── Role ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# app  = control plane (auth, admin, registry). No ClickHouse.
# zone = data plane (ingest, queries, issues, alerting). No auth surface.
# both = one process serving both. The deployed control plane runs this.
MON_ROLE=both

# ─── Identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The zone this process IS. REQUIRED on MON_ROLE=zone — env.RequireZoneIdentity
# refuses to start a data plane that inherited the fallback, because such a
# process seeds a second zone row under the control plane's name, binds its keys
# to it, and reports it on /health, with nothing in the log to say so.
MON_ZONE_SLUG=trailblaze

# The project an unset ?project selector resolves to, and the one the env master
# key files its own events under.
MON_DEFAULT_PROJECT=default

# This process's own public origin. NO DEFAULT, deliberately: it used to fall
# back to the control plane's URL, and bootstrap.ensureZone seeds a new zone's
# ingest_url AND query_url from it — so a zone that forgot to set it recorded a
# registry row pointing at the control plane, and the probe could still return
# healthy. Also builds every SSO redirect_uri.
MON_PUBLIC_URL=https://api.monitor.appleby.cloud

# Where the dashboard lives. Used for links in notifications.
MON_WEB_URL=https://monitor.appleby.cloud

# ─── HTTP ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HTTP_PORT=8080

# ─── ClickHouse (events) — data plane only ───────────────────────────────────
CLICKHOUSE_ADDR=localhost:9000
CLICKHOUSE_DATABASE=monitor
CLICKHOUSE_USERNAME=default
CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=
CLICKHOUSE_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE=2147483648

# ─── MariaDB (auth, registry, issues, alerting config) ───────────────────────
# REQUIRED in every role.
#
# ⚠️ Must be a FULLY RESOLVED literal. Lattice substitutes ${VAR} only as a whole
# value, never mid-string, so `monitor:${MARIADB_PASSWORD}@tcp(...)` is sent
# verbatim and presents as a wrong password.
#
# ⚠️ The DSN user needs privileges on BOTH schemas. Migration 110 does
# `CREATE DATABASE monitor`, but the mariadb image grants the app user rights
# only on MARIADB_DATABASE, so a fresh install needs, as root:
#     GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON monitor.* TO 'monitor'@'%'; FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
MON_DB_DSN=monitor:monitor@tcp(127.0.0.1:3336)/monitor_auth

# ─── Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The env master key. REQUIRED — the process refuses to start without it. Grants
# full ingest AND query on the default project of whichever zone it is presented
# to, so it must NOT be shared between zones.
MONITOR_API_KEY=

# Session signing. REQUIRED in production (a dev default exists and is refused
# unless MON_COOKIE_INSECURE=true).
#
# ⚠️ Must be BYTE-IDENTICAL across the control plane and every zone. A zone
# verifies control-plane-signed access tokens (middleware/session.go builds the
# user from claims, because a zone's users table is empty by design), so a
# mismatch makes every cross-zone dashboard read 401 in a loop.
MON_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=

# AES-256-GCM key, EXACTLY 32 bytes. REQUIRED in production. Encrypts SSO client
# secrets and cached IdP tokens, and — since migration 126 — notification-channel
# config, which is why a zone genuinely needs it too.
MON_CRYPTO_KEY=

# ─── Sessions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MON_COOKIE_DOMAIN=
# true = local dev: drops Secure from cookies and allows the dev-default secrets.
MON_COOKIE_INSECURE=false

# ─── First-run admin (control plane only) ────────────────────────────────────
# Empty means no admin is seeded. Ignored entirely on MON_ROLE=zone.
MON_ADMIN_EMAIL=
MON_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
MON_ALLOW_REGISTRATION=false

# ─── GitHub issue links (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Absent means the GitHub features are simply inactive — no error.
# ⚠️ Named for zone one. The webhook route is registered on EVERY data plane, so
# a second zone watching a different org still sets a variable called _TRAILBLAZE.
MON_GITHUB_TOKEN_TRAILBLAZE=
MON_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET_TRAILBLAZE=

# ─── Ingest pipeline ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BATCH_SIZE=1000
FLUSH_INTERVAL=5s
QUEUE_SIZE=100000
MAX_SSE_SUBSCRIBERS=100

# ─── Self-telemetry (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where monitor-core reports its OWN errors and activity — the appleby zone,
# like every other appleby.cloud service. Unset URL = nothing shipped; warnings
# and errors still print to stdout. Read from the PLAIN environment before
# Keyring injects anything, so a Keyring failure can itself be reported.
#
# ⚠️ MON_TELEMETRY_*, NOT MONITOR_*: MONITOR_API_KEY above is this process's
# ingest MASTER key. On Lattice map these to the globals:
#   MON_TELEMETRY_INGEST_URL=${MONITOR_APPLEBY_INGEST_URL}
#   MON_TELEMETRY_API_KEY=${MONITOR_APPLEBY_INGEST_KEY}
MON_TELEMETRY_INGEST_URL=
MON_TELEMETRY_API_KEY=
MON_TELEMETRY_ENV=production
# The zone the URL is expected to be (set it to `appleby`). Asserted once at
# boot against the destination's /health; never sent. Empty = not asserted.
MON_TELEMETRY_ZONE=
# Durable spool (a host path or named volume). Empty = memory only.
MON_TELEMETRY_SPOOL_DIR=
MON_TELEMETRY_DEBUG=false
# true = the SDK prints EVERY event as NDJSON. Local verification only.
MON_TELEMETRY_STDOUT=false

# ─── Keyring (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ Keyring's InjectEnv runs BEFORE env.Load(), so anything it supplies
# OVERRIDES the values above rather than filling gaps. A broadly-granted token
# will silently replace this zone's CLICKHOUSE_* with another zone's. Grant a
# zone's token only the secrets that zone needs.
# KEYRING_URL=https://keys.appleby.cloud
# KEYRING_ACCESS_KEY_ID=KR...
# KEYRING_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
